#!/opt/conda/bin/python
"""rs-docs — give a repository a just-the-docs site built from its docs/ folder.

The site is the repository's own docs/ folder, published by a GitHub workflow
that runs GitHub's own Pages build every time docs/ changes on the default
branch.

Subcommands:
  init [--dry-run]   lay down the site files in docs/, the workflow in
                     .github/workflows/docs.yml, and sidebar front matter on
                     every page in docs/ that has none. Refuses, changing
                     nothing, when anything is in the way. --dry-run reads
                     only and prints what init would write, every file that
                     would be published, template code in the pages, pages
                     with no known place in the sidebar, and each reason init
                     would refuse.
  check              read the docs/ tree only (no network, no docker) and
                     print one line per defect; exit 1 when there is any.
  build              build the site as GitHub will: GitHub's own Pages build
                     image (the release the workflow names), run with this
                     container's docker as the calling user on docs/ (mounted
                     read-only), into one fixed folder per work tree under
                     /workspace/.rs-docs/; then the workflow's link check on
                     the built site. Prints the folder.

init (without --dry-run) runs in a worktree only, never in the primary clone.

Exit codes: 0 done / ok; 1 defects (check), a failed build or a broken link
(build), or an internal error; 2 a refusal (init, build) or no site to check.

Wiring resolution (mirrors rs-board), used by init's one read of the upstream
mirror's record on Gitea:
  - dev BOX: GITEA_URL/GITEA_TOKEN arrive as container env.
  - dev PROJECT (supervisor): the agent_user-bearing row of the host-staged
    /workspace/.orchestrator/dev-gitea.json + its token file under
    ~/.dev-tokens/.
The token travels ONLY as the Authorization header — never argv, never
inside a URL, never in output.

Standalone by design: image-baked into both dev surfaces (in /usr/local/lib/rs,
linked onto PATH), so it cannot import cli/ modules; the site files sit
beside its resolved path in docs-site/.
"""

